# Protocol — Periodic checkpoint ({{CAMPAIGN_TITLE}})

Fires every {{CHECKPOINT_EVERY}} experiments (`exp_id % {{CHECKPOINT_EVERY}} == 0`). Stop
feature-chasing and reorient: confirm the campaign is still healthy and still pointed at the goal.

## 1. Re-anchor
Re-read {{REANCHOR_DOCS}} and `results/DISCOVERIES.md`. Is the current line of work still the best use
of effort, or has a discovery changed what's possible?

## 2. Review the scoreboard
Sort `results/scoreboard.tsv` by {{SCOREBOARD_REVIEW_SORTS}}. Where is the real progress? Which levers
are exhausted? Is the current-best genuinely ahead of the floor by more than the spread?

## 3. Hygiene checks
{{HYGIENE_CHECKS}}
<!-- e.g. every row has a result_<NN>.json; the current-best config is reproducible; no orphaned
     PROVISIONAL findings; the guardrail still behaves on known-good/known-bad inputs; diagnostics
     logs are persisted, not console-only.
     ALSO (always check these — they were added after real campaigns leaked on them):
     - NO ORPHANED RESULT: every scoreboard row / result_<NN>.json has a completed logbook/JOURNAL
       narrative AND a graded verdict (a result whose analysis was deferred is the commonest leak).
     - VERIFY GATE WIRED: .claude/settings.json registers the guard_discoveries hook (imported/relocated
       trees lose it); the current-best row's `verified` column is not blank.
     - COMPARABILITY: every row carries metric_version + data_version; no current-best compares across
       versions (re-score under the current version first).
     - UPSTREAM PREPROCESSING (promotion check): the load-bearing preprocessing feeding the current-best
       (registration / pose / normalization) is non-degenerate on the data it is applied to. A degenerate
       upstream step can pass the metric+guardrail while silently corrupting specific inputs (a real campaign
       promoted a best whose registration was mis-aligning some frames). Validate the transform, not just the
       score. -->
For the full hygiene list, run `campaign-status` (it encodes these checks).

## 4. Re-plan
Pick the {{REPLAN_HORIZON}} most promising orthogonal directions for the next block of experiments and
write them as the JOURNAL **NEXT** pointer. If progress has plateaued, trigger a literature search.
